Circulor operates blockchain-based digital product passports tracking materials across supply chains, embedding GHG emissions and ESG data into material flow. Battery Passport built on Hyperledger Fabric demonstrates compliance with EU regulations; embedded carbon footprint, recycled content percentages, and state-of-health tracking. Since 2017, Circulor has traced 150+ million batteries, 500,000 electric vehicles, across 30 global supply chains including 125+ facilities. Digital passports enable remanufacturers to verify core material provenance and composition.